# 3. AREA ONE – MINE ENTRANCE PORTAL

## Environment

Create a monumental entrance carved into the surrounding mountain rock.

The entrance should feel like the entrance to an ancient dwarven kingdom.

### Architecture

- A massive stone doorway.
- Two large carved stone pillars.
- Heavy metallic gates.
- Dwarven runes and ancient symbols.
- Decorative stone carvings.
- Torches mounted on the walls.
- Large stairs descending toward the Main Mine Hall.
- Natural rock formations surrounding the constructed entrance.

The entrance should be wide and tall enough for heavy mining carts and dwarven machinery.

### Gameplay and navigation

The player enters through this portal and immediately gains a view of the enormous mining facility.

The transition should reveal the Main Mine Hall gradually, creating a sense of scale and discovery.

Do not hide the entire main hall behind unnecessary walls.

---

# 4. AREA TWO – MAIN MINE HALL

## Highest-priority environment

This is the primary hub of the mine and one of the most important areas in the entire project.

It must be a large, spacious, highly detailed underground industrial hall.

The room should be significantly larger than the surrounding side areas.

It should combine a dwarven railway station, mining headquarters, material processing area and workers' settlement.

### A. General architecture

Create a large irregularly shaped underground chamber.

Include:
- Tall natural cave ceilings.
- Thick stone pillars.
- Large support beams.
- Carved stone floors.
- Reinforced walls.
- Iron machinery.
- Wooden platforms.
- Decorative dwarven architecture.

Some parts should look naturally excavated, while others should look carefully constructed by dwarven engineers.

Do not make the hall perfectly symmetrical.

### B. Central railway station

The center of the hall should contain a large railway hub.

Build:

- A circular railway turntable.
- Multiple tracks branching from the center.
- Mining carts.
- Cargo platforms.
- Railway switches.
- Loading and unloading areas.
- A small mechanical control station.

The railway system should lead toward the Mining Galleries and other industrial sections.

The tracks must be physically connected and correctly positioned.

Mining carts should sit properly on the rails.

### C. Heavy machinery

Add a large industrial crane or ore-lifting system.

It should include:
- Thick chains.
- Large gears.
- Metal supports.
- Suspension hooks.
- A lifting platform.
- Mechanical pulleys.

The crane should look functional rather than decorative.

### D. Dwarven workers

Create multiple dwarven workers performing different activities.

Examples:
- Workers transporting stones.
- Workers sorting minerals.
- Workers repairing machinery.
- Workers loading mining carts.
- Workers operating mechanical equipment.
- Workers using pickaxes and hammers.
- Workers carrying tools and supplies.

The hall must feel inhabited.

### E. Storage and workstations

Place:
- Wooden crates.
- Barrels.
- Ore containers.
- Tool racks.
- Workbenches.
- Anvils.
- Wooden carts.
- Material storage piles.

Create small work zones along the edges of the hall.

### F. Dwarven resting area

Integrate a modest dining and resting area into one side of the hall.

Include:
- Large wooden tables.
- Benches.
- Barrels.
- Food containers.
- Mugs.
- A fireplace.
- Weapon racks.

Do not create an additional large dining room.

The resting area should feel like a natural part of the main industrial hub.

