# 9. AREA SEVEN – GRAND CHASM HALL

## Major environmental landmark

The Grand Chasm should be an enormous underground cavern containing a deep abyss.

It should occupy a large part of the lower environment.

The space should communicate enormous scale.

### A. Natural cavern

Create:
- Huge rocky walls.
- Deep vertical drops.
- Large natural stone formations.
- Massive pillars.
- Distant cliffs.
- Atmospheric fog.
- Dark underground spaces.

The player should not be able to see the entire bottom of the abyss.

Use lighting and fog to create depth.

### B. Distant environment

Add some distant environmental structures:

- Smaller ancient bridges.
- Distant stone platforms.
- Natural rock pillars.
- Tiny lights.
- Distant waterfalls.
- Old abandoned dwarven structures.

These elements should create the impression that the cavern continues far beyond the playable area.

Not every distant structure needs to be accessible.

### C. Large open space

Do not fill the cavern with excessive objects.

The enormous open abyss is itself a major visual feature.

Preserve large negative spaces.

